				<wikidot:authorName>Potato_Launch</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2857193</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I like the idea, but it seems like something like this is Keter for sure as it alters the personalities of those affected to the point of letting skips out of containment and even placing them in the wrong containment cell, who knows what else could go wrong.</p> <p>I found it alarming, and if it wasn't for the -J I would have thought this was a serial skip.</p> <p>Neutral for the moment, just seems like a great idea that hasn't realized its full potential.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1775592#post-2552357</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1775592/scp-012-j#post-2552357</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 09 Aug 2016 08:43:31 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Accelerando</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1599414</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This could have been a lot funnier, really. The logs are just recitations of old tropes in sitcoms and stale in-jokes, instead of building off of actual Foundation canon.</p> <p>If there had been a bit of actual character establishment with a set of people instead of everyone acting like a joker, (much like an actual sitcom,) there could have been better opportunities. Maybe some satire on how impractical it is to constantly recontain 682, maybe some slightly meta banter between characters, maybe a callback to a joke earlier in the set of logs.</p> <p>For now, it's just sitcoms appearing out of nowhere.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
