					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1775592#post-2548617</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1775592/scp-012-j#post-2548617</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 05 Aug 2016 02:17:45 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Petrograd</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>455145</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1955-j">SCP-1955-J</a>, mine.</p> <p>That one only got funny because people in the comments talked me into writing the event logs.</p> <p>Edit: About this article, basically, the logs aren't funny, the fact that they aren't funny isn't itself funny, and instead of taking this in a positive or amusing direction you've just muddled it with &quot;typical&quot; SCP gore and sadness. I'm not against some dark humor, but the last log basically reads like a compulsion effect getting people killed.</p> <p>With a pop culture reference -J like this, having the idea isn't enough. &quot;What if bad sit-com but SCP?&quot; doesn't have much mileage to it. The logs are where you add your creative input. If those can make people laugh, then you'll get upvotes. If they don't, it'll sink. (Ask me how I know.)</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
